: 0}], "type": "RSLT", "_data": [{"contents": [], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}], "id": 10}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob09re7pdf01.pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 0}], "id": 0}], "type": "DWS", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Talking About unit testing"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 11}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n8le01ob09re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n8le01ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Professor:</span>\nIn the last lecture, we left off at the code coverage chapter. Let's review some important concepts. So, what do we use code coverage metrics for?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Student:</span>What code coverage metrics do is give feedback on how much of the code was tested. Knowing what parts of the code were left untested helps us determine if it's necessary to test the remaining code."}, {"time": "20700", "image": "enpe8n8le01ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Professor:</span>Exactly, it's not compulsory to test all the code. Hence, after knowing what part of the code was left untested, we need to think whether it's useful to test the rest of it or not.<br />\nOn one occasion, I decided to check if the code coverage I had tested for an application I developed was working appropriately. What the results presented was that I had only covered 60% of the code instead of the 90% I was expecting. What I concluded was that I didn't test the added error checking code; and nevertheless, the application worked fine. Therefore, there was no need for further testing.<br />\nThe code coverage metric only indicates what piece of code was tested, but it doesn't tell you how good this code is. So, we could get a high code coverage of code that's not really good. Now, to finish our review, as we discussed on unit testing, tell me how this can be related to code coverage."}, {"time": "73300", "image": "enpe8n8le01ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Student:</span> What a tester will do in a unit testing process is examine if the code behaves as expected by writing drivers and stubs, and test each individual unit code. Using this method helps to easily spot where the defects of a code are. Once we've tested the code, we can rely on the code coverage metrics to know how much code was tested and how much of it is missing."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n8le01ob09re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0}]}